From a1b2c3d4e5f60000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: han30230 <han30230@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:42:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Add joint registration completion boundary

A joint proposal was previously written participant-by-participant and execution
was started as soon as Participant::set() returned. The traffic schedule mirror
can observe those writes on different updates, which permits a conflict to be
opened against a mixed A-new/B-old view.

Stage the group registration and wait until BOTH PlanId and ItineraryVersion
for every member are observed by the fleet mirror before any command starts.
While this boundary is active, only negotiations whose local participants point
at the immediately previous/current transition and include at least one previous
plan are rejected as stale transition conflicts. External participants and
current/current conflicts retain the existing stop/quiesce/legacy-negotiation
path.

The registration wait is asynchronous. Timeout, validation failure, or a
registration mismatch restores stationary occupancy. If planned route times
become stale while waiting, the existing one-shot stale retry is reused before
falling back. No solver, search budget, or agent-count policy changes.
